WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — rce-vc (45s) Narrator River

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.729
First, many people and AI agents write at once,

2
00:00:03.729 --> 00:00:07.252
and a named check admits changes or records why.

3
00:00:07.692 --> 00:00:11.456
Second, tracking name-free functions instead of text lines

4
00:00:11.456 --> 00:00:15.350
lets unrelated edits pass together without false merge wars.

5
00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:23.152
Third, developers stay on ordinary Git while checking against one hundred thousand items takes seventy microseconds.

6
00:00:23.592 --> 00:00:28.912
When ten AI coding helpers improve ten separate functions inside one Python file,

7
00:00:28.912 --> 00:00:38.502
line-based Git panics like ten chefs fighting over one sheet of paper. Indexing individual functions lets every non-overlapping edit land cleanly.

8
00:00:38.942 --> 00:00:43.421
Teams keep their everyday Git commands while a standalone Rust engine gates

9
00:00:43.421 --> 00:00:48.615
every change in three hundred seventeen microjoules and reuses accepted conflict fixes.
